The model compiles cleanly with all QC passing. Summary of what I built:

**Object:** A potted plant — a weathered concrete cachepot with a leafy ZZ-style houseplant, sized ~0.25 m pot and ~0.57 m overall height (fits the 0.38 × 0.58 × 0.38 box).

**Structure (single root, all parts directly under it):**
- `planter` (root) — a genuinely **hollow** tapered concrete pot, built as a closed-profile CadQuery revolve with real 12 mm wall thickness, a rim lip and a 20 mm-thick base slab, converted to the y-up world frame. Concrete gray material.
- `plant` — potting soil revolved to follow the pot's interior taper (2–3 mm clearance, no wall penetration) plus domed soil surface, seven arching stems built as spline tubes, and 61 lens-sectioned leaves (pointed tip, midrib ridge, drooping camber) merged into two green-tone foliage meshes.

**Articulation:** `planter_to_plant` — REVOLUTE about the vertical axis at the root-ball centre, limits ±π, so the whole root ball and canopy turn inside the pot (the real way you rotate a plant to even out its growth).

**Support / fit:** the soil disc sits exactly on the pot's inner floor (verified contact), the soil stays within the pot's outer envelope (verified containment at rest and when turned), and foliage rises above the rim. The soil-inside-pot nesting is an intentional, element-scoped overlap allowance paired with exact contact/containment proofs.

